olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Before an engorged international break we =
have a gala weekend of derby games. Some of them are familiar, others rathe=
r longer in the waiting, others spurious in their definition but shoehorned=
 in for tea-timely email purposes. Thursday night=E2=80=99s Bigger Vase def=
eat by Ferencvaros was not a great result for angry Martin O=E2=80=99Neill=
=E2=80=99s Celtic, coming three days before the <strong>Old Firm/Glasgow de=
rby</strong> (delete as applicable according to adherence to Scottish compa=
ny law), and four days after losing to Rangers in the Old Firm/Glasgow derb=
y. In Spain, <strong>Atl=C3=A9tico v Real Madrid</strong> will see Diego Si=
meone and Jos=C3=A9 Mourinho bring the <em>morbo</em> ruckus to the sidelin=
es. A football match might actually break out, though that cannot be guaran=
teed when considering the managers involved.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Plenty of anticipation <a href=3D"https://=
ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEM=
gszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgmydUS0ukfiNlxk1LYH-u8g2UVQTrerWTd5rtmhCojKJ=
bSAZzodg_bIIzxO8QU77QSu4LS_f3fb95wEgZl19sbPDMHDY4yP2PAWHj8ihADi-oMsZ2rwklIB=
4fzZ8wTFJ7So_CYTPnSSKKivas9OZIHphYOQFOVrog2WFHZg2L04EDge7awObu5Q6EkxR9rF1UZ=
Ku7pjhEmViElGXwXNNVh2-oYZWcgcehyUqM3tQLcQM/4u5/QDlgvoAhRziWXmcnDGWmfw/h28/h=
001.B8sVl2z4rIbHiWN2_cMOzAmDug6FsRhH9S39sgwhgR8" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">=
for </a><strong><a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u0=
01.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgmydUS0uk=
fiNlxk1LYH-u8g2UVQTrerWTd5rtmhCojKJbSAZzodg_bIIzxO8QU77QSu4LS_f3fb95wEgZl19=
sbPDMHDY4yP2PAWHj8ihADi-oMsZ2rwklIB4fzZ8wTFJ7So_CYTPnSSKKivas9OZIHphYOQFOVr=
og2WFHZg2L04EDge7awObu5Q6EkxR9rF1UZKu7pjhEmViElGXwXNNVh2-oYZWcgcehyUqM3tQLc=
QM/4u5/QDlgvoAhRziWXmcnDGWmfw/h29/h001.0sWs-IBhjdrbQB0GgymwkPwSXzX96RLQY_IZ=
By_Rptc" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Millwall v West Ham</a></strong>, if not=
 from the Met police, which has set up a Section 35 dispersal zone stretchi=
ng across most of the map on the closing credits of EastEnders. Saturday=E2=
=80=99s match-up will have rung out when the fixtures came out. That four p=
oints separate the two clubs in the battle for promotion has become a side =
issue. The =E2=80=9CDockers derby=E2=80=9D, when supporters=E2=80=99 ancest=
ors worked for rival firms either side of the Thames, hasn=E2=80=99t been p=
layed since 2012, the long years since consumed by the cartoon mythology of=
 Danny Dyer, Tamer Hassan and the Rise of the Footsoldier franchise.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Talking of grudge matches, <strong>Wrexham=
 v Southampton</strong> gained extra Spygate fizz when co-owners Ryan Reyno=
lds and Rob Mac released a social media disgrace ad for their official web =
browser (!) on the =E2=80=9Cimportance of privacy=E2=80=9D. Those guys! Els=
ewhere in the Championship, <strong>Wolves and West Brom</strong> are reuni=
ted for a first league fixture in five years, a Sunday high noon kick-off t=
ime reflecting West Midlands police=E2=80=99s similar concerns to their Lon=
don counterparts after <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/=
ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEB8pAdfUJGH_TIiYQYLGktb0=
CMl5ZoWMuntS7vrAjp19OkChwbZIG96xorAyGJlweA17XcjZycbn4NB70Pdke7G-9jmNik-BY7H=
memicicX25uuntC8QhRkMBZJpvHHcebLFGFvVEKCCPfWhtYGSPy1NoXRriRuPQ8TSsVnXW2z37Q=
Y1xqe4zON7Wqoes9xxBHiGzXHgZIO8YpjdI0c-L9YFAiJXLdGoX2Q3yXgEQcQMQ/4u5/QDlgvoA=
hRziWXmcnDGWmfw/h30/h001.s2jDqK-g91UcU1_FYK6HvVu38rb4tdZj3Nm_DKtuaYc" style=
=3D"color: #0077B6;">a 2024 cup date</a>. Rather more genteel, a university=
 challenge between <strong>Oxford </strong>and <strong>Cambridge</strong>, =
and after Oxon and Cantab split the men=E2=80=99s and women=E2=80=99s Boat =
Races, there=E2=80=99s first-class honours at stake, in a battle of League =
One playoff hopefuls.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">To a couple of desperation derbies, then. =
They say you are never more than six feet away from a pest in a big city, a=
nd the same logic is true of turmoil at <strong>Manchester United</strong> =
and/or Tottenham. Did Michael Carrick shed tears after that Littlewoods Cup=
 defeat by Brighton? Who could blame him? On Sunday United really, really m=
ust beat <strong>Fulham</strong>, for whom =C3=81lvaro Arbeloa is taking on=
 the look of lame-duck manager, as well as that of a cross between General =
Zod and Rylan. If not, Carrick stares down the face of three weeks where =
=E2=80=9CUnited in crisis=E2=80=9D is blood in the water for needy hacks. M=
aybe <strong>Tottenham</strong> can provide cover. Their goal drought has b=
een mocked by try-hard pizza companies though perhaps a visit from <strong>=
Aston Villa</strong>, whose summer reboot has yielded just one point, can e=
nd Spurs=E2=80=99 hosepipe ban.</p>
