B6;">yesterday=E2=80=99s Football Daily letters</a>), but in a way that now=
 seems rather surreal. When I was a kid, my junior Sunday league team train=
ed at West Ham=E2=80=99s Chadwell Heath training ground every Friday night =
in their sports hall. In them days, anyone could drive into the car park an=
d walk through the gym to the hall =E2=80=93 and on one particular night my=
 dad dropped me and a teammate off and told us he=E2=80=99d be back in an h=
our. When we walked into the hall we were more than surprised to find that =
our team had cancelled training, with nobody else turning up, and half of t=
he West Ham first team were in there doing drills instead. With nowhere to =
go (and no mobile phones) they invited us to join in. As an Arsenal fan, I =
didn=E2=80=99t really care much for West Ham players, but their goalkeeper =
was a lovely man and spent most of the hour playing with us and encouraging=
 shots. I never forgot Ludo after that night=E2=80=9D =E2=80=93 Nicholas La=
rkin.</p></div></td></tr>
